UID:41901-1781359200-1781362800@www.torontomastergardeners.ca
SUMMARY:Demo: Container Gardening: Supporting Our Local Pollinators in Small Spaces: High Park Library
DESCRIPTION:Pollinators need a supply of nectar throughout the growing season\, so if you are planting up pots for your garden or balcony\, why not choose plants that will attract birds\, bees\, and butterflies? This demonstration will start with how to choose soil\, plants\, and containers\, and how to arrange them to maximize their positive impact on the environment. At the end of the demonstration\, materials will be shared with participants\, while supplies last.
URL:https://www.torontomastergardeners.ca/event/demo-container-gardening-supporting-our-local-pollinators-in-small-spaces-high-park-library/
LOCATION:Toronto Public Library – High Park
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Toronto Master Gardeners
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260615T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260615T200000
DTSTAMP:20260613T002927
CREATED:20260209T161310Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260209T161310Z
UID:41763-1781550000-1781553600@www.torontomastergardeners.ca
SUMMARY:Basics of urban vegetable gardening
DESCRIPTION:Growing (and eating!) your own vegetables has so many benefits. Come and discover the joy of growing your own food. You can’t beat the taste\, and you save some money while doing it. We cover all the bases including planning new garden beds\, the importance of soil\, starting seeds indoors\, crop rotation\, caring for your plants\, feeding/fertilizing and maximizing productivity by extending the growing season.
URL:https://www.torontomastergardeners.ca/event/basics-of-urban-vegetable-gardening-2/
LOCATION:Ontario
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Toronto Master Gardeners
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260617T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260617T170000
DTSTAMP:20260613T002927
CREATED:20260527T182858Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260527T192629Z
UID:42374-1781712000-1781715600@www.torontomastergardeners.ca
SUMMARY:Balcony and container gardening
DESCRIPTION:Apartment\, condominium and townhouse dwellers deserve to have beautiful and bountiful outdoor gardens too! We’ll deal with practical tricks for successful gardening “above ground”\, taking into account your special challenges\, share design ideas\, and recommend plant choices\, including annuals\, perennials\, bulbs\, shrubs\, trees\, edibles and native plants. \nHosted by Feed Scarborough Community Garden.  Register at https://forms.gle/EaqES2JiNexYSdtx8
URL:https://www.torontomastergardeners.ca/event/balcony-and-container-gardening-4/
LOCATION:Feed Scarborough\, 3595 St. Clair Avenue East\, Scarborough
END:VEVENT
